.TH CONFERENCING 1 "June 2026" "RTS2" "User Commands"

.SH NAME
conferencing \- real-time audio conferencing application

.SH SYNOPSIS
.B conferencing
[\fIaddress\fR]
[\fB--hw\fR]
[\fB--sim\fR]
[\fB--no-udp\fR]
[\fB--np\fR]
[\fB--ms\fR \fImilliseconds\fR]
[\fB--split\fR \fIcount\fR]
[\fB--fifo\fR \fIsize\fR]

.SH DESCRIPTION
.B conferencing
is a real-time audio conferencing application that records audio,
processes it through a configurable processing pipeline, optionally
transmits it over UDP, and plays the received audio.

The processing pipeline consists of:

.RS
Recorder →
Low-pass filter →
Echo cancellation →
μ-law encoder →
UDP transmit →
UDP receive →
μ-law decoder →
Playback
.RE

Audio is captured in configurable hardware blocks and internally split
into smaller processing blocks for fine-grained scheduling.

.SH OPTIONS

.TP
.BI address
Destination IPv4 address used for UDP transmission.
Examples:
127.0.0.1,
192.168.1.100.

.TP
.B --hw
Run using physical audio hardware (default).

.TP
.B --sim
Run using simulated audio input/output.

.TP
.B --no-udp
Disable UDP networking.
Audio is looped back locally.

.TP
.B --np
Disable audio processing.
Recorder connects directly to transmitter/playback.

.TP
.BI --ms " milliseconds"
Size of the audio hardware callback in milliseconds.

For example:

.RS
5 ms  = 240 samples

10 ms = 480 samples

20 ms = 960 samples
.RE

.TP
.BI --split " count"
Number of internal processing blocks created from one hardware block.

The processing block size is computed as

.RS
process_frames = frames_per_buffer / split
.RE

Example:

.RS
--ms 10 --split 10

480-sample hardware block

10 × 48-sample processing blocks
.RE

.TP
.BI --fifo " size"
Maximum number of audio blocks stored in each FIFO.

.SH EXAMPLES

Run locally using loopback networking:

.nf
conferencing 127.0.0.1 --ms 10 --split 10 --fifo 20
.fi

Run using hardware with a remote receiver:

.nf
conferencing 192.168.50.189 --ms 10 --split 10 --fifo 20
.fi

Run in simulation mode:

.nf
conferencing --sim --ms 20 --split 5
.fi

Disable processing:

.nf
conferencing --np --no-udp
.fi

.SH AUDIO PIPELINE

For

.nf
--ms 10 --split 10
.fi

the application operates as

.nf
Recorder       480 samples
      ↓
10 × 48-sample FIFO blocks
      ↓
Low-pass
      ↓
Echo cancellation
      ↓
μ-law encoding
      ↓
Transmit
      ↓
UDP packet (480 samples)
      ↓
Receive
      ↓
10 × 48-sample FIFO blocks
      ↓
μ-law decoding
      ↓
Playback (480 samples)
.fi

.SH FILES

.TP
.B timing_report.csv
Execution timing statistics.

.TP
.B fifo_occupancy.csv
FIFO occupancy over time.

.TP
.B queue_latency.csv
FIFO queue latency measurements.

.TP
.B network_jitter.csv
Network latency and jitter measurements.

.SH EXIT STATUS

.TP
0
Successful execution.

.TP
1
Invalid command-line arguments or initialization failure.

